---
title: Sitemap
layout: home
description: Every page on the site as one tree, generated from the same array the navigation is built from — so it cannot drift out of date.
eyebrow: Pages
source: src/components/sitemap.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap" style="padding-top: 1.5rem; --im-section-gap: 1.5rem">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Pages · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<section class="im-section im-wrap-wide">
	<div class="im-collbar">
		<p class="im-caption" data-index="tree" style="margin: 0">Everything</p>
		<p class="im-cluster" style="--im-cluster-gap: .375rem"><button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button" onclick="document.querySelectorAll('.im-sitemap details').forEach(d=>d.open=true)">Expand all</button><button class="im-btn im-btn-sm" type="button" onclick="document.querySelectorAll('.im-sitemap details').forEach(d=>d.open=false)">Collapse all</button></p>
		<p class="im-snipcard-meta"><span>{{sitemap.length}} sections</span><a class="im-card-cta" href="/sitemap.xml">sitemap.xml {{icon "external-link"}}</a></p>
	</div>

	<div class="im-sitemap-cols" style="--im-sitemap-cols: 3">
		<ul class="im-sitemap">
			<li>
				<span class="im-sitemap-node im-sitemap-branch">{{icon "file-text"}}Pages<span class="im-sitemap-count">6</span></span>
				<ul>
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="/pages/about/">{{icon "user"}}About</a></li>
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="/pages/now/">{{icon "clock"}}Now</a></li>
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="/pages/contact/">{{icon "mail"}}Contact</a></li>
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="/pages/membership/">{{icon "credit-card"}}Membership</a></li>
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="/pages/auth/">{{icon "log-in"}}Sign in / Sign up</a></li>
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="/pages/sitemap/">{{icon "list"}}Sitemap</a></li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			{{#each sitemap}}
			{{#unless title}}{{#each items}}<li><a class="im-sitemap-node im-sitemap-branch" href="{{url}}">{{icon icon}}{{label}}</a></li>{{/each}}{{else}}
			<li>
				<details open>
				<summary><span class="im-sitemap-node im-sitemap-branch">{{icon icon}}{{title}}<span class="im-sitemap-count">{{count}}</span></span></summary>
				<ul{{#match count ">" 6}} data-more{{/match}}>
					{{#each items}}
					{{#if children}}
					<li>
						<details>
						<summary><span class="im-sitemap-node im-sitemap-branch">{{icon icon}}{{label}}<span class="im-sitemap-count">{{children.length}}</span></span></summary>
						<ul>
							{{#each children}}<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="{{url}}">{{icon "file-text"}}{{label}}</a></li>{{/each}}
						</ul>
						</details>
					</li>
					{{else}}
					<li><a class="im-sitemap-node" href="{{url}}">{{icon "file-text"}}{{label}}</a></li>
					{{/if}}
					{{/each}}
				</ul>
				{{#match count ">" 6}}<button class="im-sitemap-more" type="button" onclick="this.previousElementSibling.setAttribute('data-open','');this.hidden=true">Show all {{count}}</button>{{/match}}
				</details>
			</li>
			{{/unless}}
			{{/each}}
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>Generated, not written</h2>
		<p>The tree above iterates the <em>same array</em> the side navigation is built from. Adding a page adds a row here and there is nothing to remember — which is the only kind of sitemap that stays true, because a hand-written one is wrong within a month and then actively misleads.</p>

		<h2>Rules, not characters</h2>
		<p>The branches are drawn with two pseudo-elements per item rather than with dashes or box-drawing characters. A screen reader is handed a plain nested list and nothing else, and the lines stay one pixel at any zoom. The <strong>last</strong> child's vertical stops at its own centre — that half-height rule is the whole reason a tree looks finished rather than cut off.</p>
		{{{{code "css"}}}}
.im-sitemap li::before {           /* the vertical, full height */
	position: absolute;
	inset: 0 auto 0 0;
	width: 1px;
	background-color: var(--im-line);
}

.im-sitemap li:last-child::before { /* …except on the last one */
	bottom: auto;
	height: calc(var(--im-tree-row) / 2);
}
		{{{{/code}}}}

		<h2>Two sitemaps, two readers</h2>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th></th><th>This page</th><th><code>sitemap.xml</code></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><th>For</th><td>A person who is lost</td><td>A crawler</td></tr>
				<tr><th>Shows</th><td>Structure, grouped, with counts</td><td>Every URL, flat, with dates</td></tr>
				<tr><th>In Ghost</th><td>A page on the theme</td><td>Generated by Ghost, no theme involved</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
		<p>Both should exist and neither replaces the other. Link the XML one from here, as above — it is the only place on a site where that link is useful to anybody.</p>

		<h2>Marking what is behind the wall</h2>
		<p><code>data-locked</code> on a node draws a small lock after the label, from the same <code>--im-lock-glyph</code> the <a href="/collections/video/card/">thumbnails</a> use. A sitemap that silently lists members-only pages sends people to a gate without warning them; one that hides them is lying about what the site contains.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-sitemap</code></td><td>The tree. A plain nested <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> — the rules are drawn, the structure is real.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-sitemap-branch</code></td><td>A folder rather than a page. It may be a <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> when nothing lives at that URL.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-sitemap-count</code></td><td>How many pages are under it.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-sitemap-cols</code></td><td>Multi-column on a wide window, with <code>break-inside: avoid</code> so a branch is never split across a column boundary.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
